From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:16:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nb/intel/haswell: Set the maximum non-turbo ratio before
 raminit

Ramstage sets the CPU ratio after raminit, so until then the CPU runs at
the ratio it comes out of reset with. Broadwell sets the maximum
non-turbo ratio in romstage with set_max_freq(), which Haswell has but
never calls. Call it before raminit.

set_max_freq() now enables Enhanced SpeedStep first, which P-state
requests need (ramstage applies the eist option later, as before), and
reports the ratio it found and whether the new one took effect within
1 ms.

TEST=Built for the ThinkPad W541 with mrc.bin and with the native RAM
init.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/cpu/intel/haswell/romstage.c         | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++--
 src/northbridge/intel/haswell/romstage.c |  7 +++++++
 2 files changed, 28 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/cpu/intel/haswell/romstage.c b/src/cpu/intel/haswell/romstage.c
index b54cb6204..14be3e59a 100644
--- a/src/cpu/intel/haswell/romstage.c
+++ b/src/cpu/intel/haswell/romstage.c
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 #include <console/console.h>
 #include <cpu/intel/haswell/haswell.h>
 #include <cpu/x86/msr.h>
+#include <delay.h>
 #include <option.h>
 #include <types.h>
 
@@ -25,11 +26,29 @@ void set_max_freq(void)
 		perf_ctl.lo = msr.lo & 0xff00;
 	}
 
+	const unsigned int before = (rdmsr(IA32_PERF_STATUS).lo >> 8) & 0xff;
+
+	/* P-state requests need Enhanced SpeedStep; ramstage applies the eist option */
+	msr = rdmsr(IA32_MISC_ENABLE);
+	msr.lo |= (1 << 16);
+	wrmsr(IA32_MISC_ENABLE, msr);
+
 	perf_ctl.hi = 0;
 	wrmsr(IA32_PERF_CTL, perf_ctl);
 
-	printk(BIOS_DEBUG, "CPU: frequency set to %d MHz\n",
-	       ((perf_ctl.lo >> 8) & 0xff) * CPU_BCLK);
+	const unsigned int ratio = (perf_ctl.lo >> 8) & 0xff;
+
+	/* The transition takes some microseconds: wait for it, at most 1 ms */
+	unsigned int current = before;
+	for (unsigned int i = 0; i < 100 && current != ratio; i++) {
+		udelay(10);
+		current = (rdmsr(IA32_PERF_STATUS).lo >> 8) & 0xff;
+	}
+
+	printk(BIOS_DEBUG, "CPU: frequency set to %u MHz, was %u MHz\n",
+	       ratio * CPU_BCLK, before * CPU_BCLK);
+	if (current != ratio)
+		printk(BIOS_DEBUG, "CPU: still at %u MHz after 1 ms\n", current * CPU_BCLK);
 }
 
 /*
diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/romstage.c b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/romstage.c
index 1691d7989..898ede1f9 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/romstage.c
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/romstage.c
@@ -58,6 +58,13 @@ void mainboard_romstage_entry(void)
 
 	report_platform_info();
 
+	/*
+	 * Ramstage sets the CPU ratio, so raminit runs at the one the CPU
+	 * comes out of reset with. Set the maximum non-turbo ratio now, as
+	 * Broadwell does.
+	 */
+	set_max_freq();
+
 	if (CONFIG(INTEL_TXT))
 		intel_txt_romstage_init();
 
-- 
2.43.0

